This file describes system calls that application programs can make. There
are not very many system calls, and some are only optimizations that do not
normally have any observable effect.


=== I/O functions ===

* Set of capabilities to receive messages from, including the address to
place the received message.

* Set of capabilities to send messages from, including the address of the
message to be sent.

* Whether to send/receive all or any.

* Locks to acquire and/or release, all at once.

* Set of capabilities to be discarded.

* Blocking or non-blocking.

* Hard yield flag. This is a hint for scheduling.

(The usual way for a process to terminate itself is to specify a blocking
wait for all capabilities in an empty set. A process can also terminate
itself by discarding all usable capabilities.)


=== Create capabilities ===

You can create one or more capabilities that this process can then send to
other processes, in order to be able to communicate with them by the use of
that capability. (It needs an existing capability to send it through.)


