=== Memory mapping ===

A memory mapping must be given by someone else (such as the kernel). Each
mapping can be read/write or read-only; a read/write mapping cannot be
transferred without giving up your own access, but a read-only mapping can
be transferred while retaining your own access. Also, some mappings will
allow capabilities to be stored in them while others (such as mappings of
video memory) cannot contain capabilities. You can convert any read/write
mapping that you have access to, into read-only.


=== Process name ===

Sets a process name for debugging purposes in the system special screen
(the process name does not do anything else and cannot be read by
anything). It can fail for various reasons (including not having permission
to set it for the specified process, the name being invalid, the kernel
being compiled in such a way that it doesn't use this, etc), in which case
nothing happens; there is no error code to indicate failure.

(This might become unnecessary, if there will be a better way to do what
this is intended for.)
